prompt:
Expand and simplify completely: \begin{align*}
x\left(x(1+x)+2x\right)-3(x^2-x+2)
\end{align*}

answer:
Expand and simplify each term:

x(x(1+x)+2x) - 3(x^2-x+2)
\begin{align*}
&= x(1 + x + 2x) - 3(x^2 - x + 2) \\
&= x(3x + 1) - 3(x^2 - x + 2)
\end{align*}

Distribute the 3:

\begin{align*}
&= 3x^2 + x - 3x^2 + 3x - 6
\end{align*}

Combine like terms:

\begin{align*}
&= (3x^2 - 3x^2) + (x + 3x) - 6 \\
&= 4x - 6
\end{align*}

So the final answer is:

\boxed{4x - 6}

